# Edit Modbus read ranges in their own module settings dialog

Draft · lane full · spec rev 6 · gauntlet green at 40b290a

## Why
Modbus read ranges are edited in a separate module settings dialog (`:module`), so loading a module from a device-config file keeps that file's ranges.

## Scenarios
The 6 scenarios of #398: S1 Change read ranges on a running client · S2 A malformed range is refused · S3 Leaving the dialog without saving · S4 Loading a module keeps the device file's ranges · S5 Editing a module keeps its ranges · S6 No module settings on a monitor tab

## Stages
- [x] Land spec (c0ffee0) <!-- s0 -->
- [x] Module settings dialog (c0ffee1) <!-- s1 blocked-by s0 -->
- [x] Apply read ranges at runtime (c0ffee2) <!-- s2 blocked-by s1 -->
- [x] Setup dialog without ranges (c0ffee3) <!-- s3 blocked-by s2 -->

## Review here
- on the branch: Land spec, Module settings dialog, Apply read ranges at runtime, Setup dialog without ranges — inline comments on their files are answered before the next stop
- later stages land after their review and the user's approval

## Architecture
4 new, 3 changed components in ferrowl; new ModuleSettingsDialog opened by `:module`, confirm queued as a PendingAction and applied in refresh

| Component | Kind | Crate › module | Change | Role |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ModuleSettingsDialog` | struct | ferrowl › module::modbus::settings_dialog | new | four `RangeSpec` inputs (holding, input, coils, discrete), live error box, close confirmation; `resolve` → `Result<ReadRanges, String>`, `confirm` → `Option<ReadRanges>` |
| `RangeSpec` | struct | ferrowl › module::modbus::settings_dialog | new | `Validate` impl over `check_range_spec` for one range input |
| `ModbusModuleView::apply_read_ranges` | fn | ferrowl › module::modbus::view::mutate | new | async, `&mut self`; writes one `ReadRanges` to the device config and the running module |
| `ModbusViewOverlay` | enum | ferrowl › module::modbus::view | changed | new `Settings(Box<ModuleSettingsDialog>)` variant |
| `PendingAction` | enum | ferrowl › module::modbus::view::overlay | changed | new `SetReadRanges(ReadRanges)` variant, applied in refresh |
| `ModbusCmd` | enum | ferrowl › module::modbus::view | changed | new `Module` variant, 13 commands |

Public surface:
- `:module` command (Modbus client/server tabs)

Closes #398
